  "habitat": "Reed beds, rank grassland, cultivations and vleis, including urban reed beds. In winter it forms nomadic flocks.",
  "summary": "A common resident. The breeding male is red above, on the upper breast and the vent, with the front and the rest of the underparts black and the wings brown. The crown is black, not red. The female and non-breeding male are warm brown with a streaked breast. The summer call is a wheezy, spluttering zik-zik-zik and zayzayzayzayzay. The Kemp paper name Red Bishop and the code VB were left unchanged.",
